    {
      "id": 141809,
      "name": "jajd2c",
      "username": "jajd2c",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/a88e4f/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2015-05-21T07:46:06.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>1. Any hero equipment works for Unity's power.</p><p>2. Unity's bots are hero targets.</p><p>3. Yes, the Environment can choose the Villain for the target with the highest HP.</p><p>4. Each hero has a turn of his/her own, and they take those turns in order as set at the start of the game. One common way to do this is to start with the hero nearest to the villain, and then activate the other heroes going clockwise around the table.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I hope this helps.</p>",
      "post_number": 2,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:18:58.627Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 13037,
