    {
      "id": 141811,
      "name": "Ameena",
      "username": "Ameena",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-05-21T12:26:24.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>1 - It doesn't specify that the equipment must come from Unity's deck, therefore you can destroy any card in play which has the \"equipment\" keyword.</p><p>2 - Any card in a hero deck is a hero card. Any card with hp is a target. Therefore a card with hp in a hero deck is a hero target :).</p><p>3 - If it just says it hits \"the target with the highest hp\" then yes, it can hit the villain if they have the highest hp. If it excluded villains it'd probably say \"hero target\".</p><p>4 - Turn order is decided at the start of the game and remains the same for the whole time (unless you're playing the Wager Master but his whole thing is messing with the rules). Villain always goes first, then heroes in the same order every time, then the environment.</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:18:58.764Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
